Subject: menus: hide the rows that cannot work on iOS

docs/ios-deadlist.md's "HIDE THE ROW" disposition, applied. Each row here is
one a player can reach today and that either cannot do anything or actively
harms them; the code behind each is left exactly as it is.

  Check for Updates   replaces the running executable (update.c:879 ends in
                      execv), which a signed, read-only app bundle cannot do.
  Send Crash Report   the upload runs on the MAIN thread inside the crash
                      (crashreport.c:309 from system.c:294). With curl on
                      (D-010) crashReportCanSend() answers true again, so the
                      row would now work - and that is exactly the problem:
                      a blocking https POST from a signal handler is not a
                      thing to hand a player. Stays hidden pending Q-012.
                      The report itself is untouched: crashReportSave/Scan and
                      the 200-line ring are file I/O and keep working, and the
                      iOS shell adds the signal handler Apple platforms never
                      had (crash.c:324).
  Exit Game           an iOS app does not quit itself, and a row that looks as
                      though it will is worse than no row.
  Dump All Assets     writes gigabytes into the user's Documents container; the
                      app is killed for disk pressure or the phone fills up.
                      The CLI flags still work on the macOS oracle, which is
                      where anyone dumping assets actually is.
  Mods: Recording     the recorder is compiled out (patch 0011: system() is
                      API_UNAVAILABLE(ios) and there is no second binary to
                      spawn). It is the last page in the Dab's Mod chain, so
                      ending the chain at Missions is what takes it off the
                      phone.

NOT hidden any more: **Community Packs**. It was on this list until patch 0040
gave the iOS build a real libcurl (D-010), which is what community.c:444/602
needed; the row and its one-tap PD Plus HD install are back on iOS and visionOS
and are verified there (M-024, M-025). Ghost Trials' online rows were never
hidden by this patch at all - they gate themselves on ghostnetIsAvailable()
(ghostnet.c:1473), so they came back with curl on their own.

Every hunk is `#ifndef PLATFORM_IOS` (or one `#ifdef`) around an existing array
entry; no other platform's menus change by a byte.

diff --git a/port/src/optionsmenu.c b/port/src/optionsmenu.c
index f953d9c6b..08bc1678e 100644
--- a/port/src/optionsmenu.c
+++ b/port/src/optionsmenu.c
@@ -5724,7 +5724,16 @@ struct menudialogdef g_ExtendedDabsModMissionMenuDialog = {
 	g_ExtendedDabsModMissionMenuItems,
 	NULL,
 	MENUDIALOGFLAG_LITERAL_TEXT,
+	// Recording is the last page in the chain, and on iOS there is no recorder
+	// to configure: record.c is compiled out because system() is
+	// API_UNAVAILABLE(ios) and there is no second binary to spawn anyway
+	// (patch 0011, docs/ios-deadlist.md §1). Ending the chain here is what
+	// takes the page off the phone; nothing else in the file changes.
+#ifdef PLATFORM_IOS
+	NULL,
+#else
 	&g_ExtendedDabsModRecordingMenuDialog,
+#endif
 };
 
 struct menudialogdef g_ExtendedDabsModDisplayMenuDialog = {
@@ -7024,6 +7033,11 @@ struct menuitem g_ExtendedTexturePackMenuItems[] = {
 		0,
 		NULL,
 	},
+	// Dump All Assets writes gigabytes into the user's Documents container and
+	// then the app is killed for disk pressure, or the phone fills up
+	// (docs/ios-deadlist.md §6). The CLI flags still work on the macOS oracle,
+	// which is where anybody dumping assets actually is.
+#ifndef PLATFORM_IOS
 	{
 		MENUITEMTYPE_SELECTABLE,
 		0,
@@ -7040,6 +7054,7 @@ struct menuitem g_ExtendedTexturePackMenuItems[] = {
 		0,
 		menuhandlerAssetDumpStatus,
